    <GaugingStation location="Coytrahen" name="Llynfi" number="58007">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Flat V weir and velocity area station. Flow altered by industrial/agricultural abstraction and some effluent returns.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Weir 1:20 cross slopes; upstream 1:2; downstream 1:5, bankfull channel width 9.1m. Station in steep valley with flows fairly well contained. Flashy response so obtaining high flow gaugings problematic.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Flat V weir and velocity area station. Bankfull channel width 9.1m.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in October 2018 (WINFAP Files v7). Ratings reviewed in 2022 and data reprocessed from 1982.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Flow influenced by industrial/agricultural abstraction, some effluent returns. The last operational coal mines in this area closed in 1985. Minewater recovery is understood to have occurred by the late 1980s. Mine dewatering increased low flows and mines may have provided some attenuation in flood events.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Coal Measures, some Boulder Clay and alluvium in valley. Mainly peaty soils, seasonally wet. Upland area with livestock farming, significant forest cover and urban development in valleys.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">EI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED. Good fit to the available gaugings." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Gauged above QMED and all recorded flows within bank." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
